# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets — never commit these. The Supabase service-role key bypasses every
# row-level-security policy in the portal database; it belongs in Vercel's
# environment variables and nowhere else.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Source video, kept out on purpose.
#
# These are the ~110MB of raw generation output the scroll sequences were made
# FROM. The frames they produced are committed under web/public/, which is what
# the site actually serves, so nothing here is needed to build or deploy — and
# Vercel re-clones the repo on every build, so carrying them would slow every
# deploy for no gain.
#
# They still live in this folder on the working machine. If they should be
# backed up, SharePoint is the right home for video; if they must be versioned,
# use Git LFS rather than committing them directly.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.avi
# The one exception: a film the site SERVES, not source. The chapters
# prototype (/commercial?mode=chapters) plays this 9.6MB encode of the camp
# sequence; it has to deploy with public/ like the frames do.
!web/public/campframes/camp-chapters.mp4

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local QA artefacts
.qa/
shots/

# Raw "Us in Action" drop from SharePoint, kept out on purpose.
#
# This folder holds Ben's unfiltered crew photos and videos. Two of them can
# never be published (a factory-interior shot and one where a supplier's
# window-film branding is readable), so the folder as a whole stays off the
# public repo. The audited, optimized selection is committed under
# web/public/action/ — that is what the site serves.
us in action/
